:''This article is about the Cat Unit. For the enemy, see [[Luke (Enemy)]].''
'''Luke''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be obtained by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Street Fighter Collaboration Event/Red Team Gacha Drop|Street Fighter Collaboration Event]]. He was added in [[Version 11.9 Update|Version 11.9]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 681
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Luke
|name2 = Luke CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Luke CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Think of Luke as a Street Fighter edition of [[Baby Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Lord Gao]] - high range, [[Strong Against]] traited enemies, and 5% chance to strike a Savage Blow, though he has lower range and lack of wave immunity, but has [[Shield Piercing]] in exchange.

Luke is overall a good ranged unit. He can safely attack enemies from his high range, with nearly 8k DPS against traited and 102,000 Effective Health at Level 30, and additional 5% chance of Savage Blow, which like Gao's crit provides extra damage every now and then. His high health also allows him to survive heavy attacks.

Luke also has quick movement speed. However, his high speed could cause him to step into the enemy's territory when the Cat Cannon is fired, to his own detriment.

Luke's [[Shield Piercing]] ability makes him a good generalist against long-ranged [[Shield|Shielded]] [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies such as [[Wicked Face]], [[Fallen Bear]] and [[Lord of Ruin Jagando]], if Shield Piercing ever activates. However, his rapid attacks can still deal a lot of damage to [[Shield]]s. The problem is that Luke also lacks [[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]], meaning [[Surge Attack#Death Surge|Aftermaths]] will harm or kill him.

